# EXAMPLE ONLY: not used in simulation. Transport settings for a real
# Pixhawk-class flight controller talking to a companion computer.
# In SITL the client connects over UDP to 127.0.0.1:8888 and none of this applies.
#
# Serial link (e.g. TELEM2 -> companion UART), agent started with:
#   MicroXRCEAgent serial --dev /dev/ttyAMA0 -b 921600
UXRCE_DDS_CFG 102        # 102 = TELEM2
SER_TEL2_BAUD 921600
MAV_1_CONFIG 0           # free TELEM2 from MAVLink if it was assigned there
#
# Ethernet alternative (Pixhawk 6X etc.), agent started with:
#   MicroXRCEAgent udp4 -p 8888
# UXRCE_DDS_CFG 1000      # Ethernet
# UXRCE_DDS_AG_IP <companion IPv4 as int32>
# UXRCE_DDS_PRT 8888
